---
import SiteLayout from "../../layouts/SiteLayout.astro";
import Playground from "../../components/Playground";
---
<SiteLayout locale="en" active="playground" title="TypeNN Playground" description="Edit two small matrices and execute MatMul, Add, or ReLU with the actual TypeNN runtime in your browser.">
  <article class="playground-page">
    <nav class="breadcrumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href="/">TypeNN</a><span>/</span><span>Playground</span></nav>
    <header class="page-heading"><p class="eyebrow">Run TypeNN in your browser</p><h1>Tensor Playground</h1><p class="lead">Change the matrix values, choose an operation and backend, then run it through the TypeNN runtime bundled with this site.</p></header>
    <Playground locale="en" client:only="react" />
    <div class="playground-disclosure"><p><strong>What this runs:</strong> the shipped TypeNN build and its TypeShade runtime. It is not a JavaScript reimplementation or a mock result.</p><p>The example is intentionally small. Runtime startup includes backend preparation; this page does not report its duration as a benchmark. Automatic mode tries WebGPU and falls back to CPU. WebGL2 must be selected explicitly.</p></div>
  </article>
</SiteLayout>
